# Line endings, decided here rather than left to whatever a reader's git is
# configured with. Windows checks out with core.autocrlf=true by default, which
# rewrites every line of every text file on the way to disk.
#
# The recorded runs are a record, not source. An events.jsonl whose lines gained
# a carriage return is no longer the file the run wrote, and the artifact's whole
# claim is that these are the bytes the experiments produced. The same goes for
# the corpus: a ProVerif model is fed to a solver, and the reference JSON is
# compared byte for byte against what a run emitted.
*.jsonl -text
*.json  -text
*.pv    -text
*.spthy -text
*.yaml  -text
*.yml   -text

# Source and prose are ordinary text; a reader editing them on Windows should
# get Windows endings and git should normalise on the way back in.
*.py    text
*.md    text
*.js    text
*.css   text
*.html  text
*.toml  text
*.txt   text

# Binary, and named so no heuristic has to guess.
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.pdf   binary
